y handling for RSVP fields (Phi, V, S) on 2D/3D lattices.</div><div class="cm-line"><br></div><div class="cm-line">Purpose:</div><div class="cm-line">- Supports reflective, periodic, and open boundary conditions.</div><div class="cm-line">- Ensures consistent evolution for core solvers and simulations.</div><div class="cm-line"><br></div><div class="cm-line">Inputs:</div><div class="cm-line">- Field array (Phi, V, or S)</div><div class="cm-line">- bc_type: 'reflective', 'periodic', or 'open'</div><div class="cm-line"><br></div><div class="cm-line">Outputs:</div><div class="cm-line">- Field array with boundary conditions applied</div><div class="cm-line"><br></div><div class="cm-line">Testing Focus:</div><div class="cm-line">- Correct mirroring for reflective BC</div><div class="cm-line">- Wrap-around for periodic BC</div><div class="cm-line">- Zero-padding for open BC</div><div class="cm-line">"""</div><div class="cm-line">from __future__ import annotations</div><div class="cm-line">import numpy as np</div><div class="cm-line"><br></div><div class="cm-line"><br></div><div class="cm-line">def apply_boundary(field: np.ndarray, bc_type: str = 'periodic') -&gt; np.ndarray:</div><div class="cm-line">    """Apply boundary conditions to a field array."""</div><div class="cm-line">    field_bc = field.copy()</div><div class="cm-line"><br></div><div class="cm-line">    if bc_type == 'reflective':</div><div class="cm-line">        # Mirror edges</div><div class="cm-line">        field_bc[0,:] = field_bc[1,:]</div><div class="cm-line">        field_bc[-1,:] = field_bc[-2,:]</div><div class="cm-line">        field_bc[:,0] = field_bc[:,1]</div><div class="cm-line">        field_bc[:,-1] = field_bc[:,-2]</div><div class="cm-line"><br></div><div class="cm-gap" style="height: 462px;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section></section></div></div></div></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="f27b5c8a-3dcd-466b-823b-f864ebceb43d" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-mini" data-aria-hidden="true" aria-hidden="true"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="133">âœ… Created <strong data-start="10" data-end="38"><code data-start="12" data-end="36">boundary_conditions.py</code></strong> â€” supports reflective, periodic, and open boundaries for Î¦, ğ’—, S fields, with demo harness.</p>
