break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="236">Perfect â€” the four modules youâ€™ve drafted (<code data-start="43" data-end="62">semantic_phase.py</code>, <code data-start="64" data-end="81">fpc_dynamics.py</code>, <code data-start="83" data-end="96">data_viz.py</code>, and <code data-start="102" data-end="115">io_utils.py</code>) together already form a <strong data-start="141" data-end="171">coherent, modular backbone</strong> for what we can formally call the <strong data-start="206" data-end="235">RSVP Analysis Suite (RAS)</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="238" data-end="490">If we complete it with a <code data-start="263" data-end="274">config.py</code> file (plus a <code data-start="288" data-end="301">__init__.py</code> for package registration), youâ€™ll have a <strong data-start="343" data-end="381">ready-to-import scientific toolkit</strong> that can run local RSVP/FPC experiments with reproducibility, diagnostics, and visualization out of the box.</p>
<p data-start="492" data-end="552">Hereâ€™s a clean, minimal <code data-start="516" data-end="527">config.py</code> to finalize the suite:</p>
